law.text:
The following classes of insurance can be written by mutual assessment life, accident and sickness insurers: Category A
Life insurance as defined in § 38.2-102;
Industrial life insurance as defined in § 38.2-104; and
Accident and sickness insurance as defined in § 38.2-109 except Medicare supplement insurance as defined in § 38.2-3600. Category B
Credit life insurance as defined in § 38.2-103;
Variable life insurance as defined in § 38.2-105;
Credit accident and sickness insurance as defined in § 38.2-108; and
Medicare supplement insurance as defined in § 38.2-3600. Category C
Annuities as defined in § 38.2-106; and
Variable annuities as defined in § 38.2-107.
